cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use reconcile-mcp in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "reconcile-mcp: Model Context Protocol server for ISO 20022 cash reconciliation"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that matches expected payments (pain.001
  credit transfers) against observed bank-statement entries (camt.053) and
  returns an explainable reconciliation: ten tools for exact, partial,
  one-to-many, many-to-one and subset-sum matching, single-pair explanation,
  probabilistic name and FX-drift amount comparison, adapters for both
  message families and deterministic sandbox scenarios.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
    email: sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
version: "0.0.5"
date-released: "2026-08-29"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/reconcile-mcp"
url: "https://reconcile-mcp.com"
keywords:
  - ISO 20022
  - reconciliation
  - camt.053
  - pain.001
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - AI agents
  - treasury
